// Whether a local list may be freed by the function that declares it. All
// three conditions must hold, and each one is a proof obligation:
//   * it is declared in this function, as a list, and not exported -- a
//     parameter, an import or an element is somebody else's;
//   * every store into it is a list literal, so the list is one this function
//     made and nothing else named it first;
//   * no use of it keeps it (walk/): it is not returned, not stored in another
//     list or an export, not assigned to another name, and not passed to
//     anything that keeps it.
// That is what makes the free at the function's exit unable to leave a
// dangling reference. The shallow free never touches the elements, which may
// be shared with anything.

// The body of a function: every statement, then the return clause, whose value
// goes to the caller and so is kept.
esc_func(int fn, string nm) {
  int r = esc_block(l2_of(fn), nm);
  if(i1_of(fn) >= 0) {
    r = r | esc_expr(i1_of(fn), nm, 1);
  }
} return int r;
